# No relaunch IDs in onchain comments

Verified `src/` source lives on explorers for the life of the deployment. Do not mention relaunch ticket IDs (`R29`, `R42`, `R45`, …) in comments or NatSpec. Write the durable reason instead.

Specs, tests, PRs, `script/` comments, and `AGENTS.md` may use R-ids.

```solidity
// BAD — ticket jargon frozen into verified source
/// @notice Hardcoded in the R29 style; the oracle exposes no `decimals()`.

// GOOD — the reason, not the ticket
/// @notice Hardcoded because the oracle exposes no `decimals()`.
```
